Section 11. How to Disable Cookies

Users may manage, block, or delete cookies stored on their devices through their browser settings or by using the consent management tools available through Prompt Studio.

Disabling certain cookies may affect the operation of some Platform features.

11.1 Browser Settings

Most modern browsers allow users to:

* View stored cookies.
* Delete individual cookies.
* Delete all cookies.
* Block third-party cookies.
* Block all cookies.
* Configure exceptions for specific websites.
* Request confirmation before storing new cookies.

The method for accessing these options depends on the browser used.

11.2 Supported Browsers

Users may consult their browser’s official instructions for managing cookies.

Common browsers include:

* Google Chrome.
* Mozilla Firefox.
* Microsoft Edge.
* Safari.
* Opera.
* Brave.

Instructions may vary between versions.

11.3 Manual Deletion

Users may delete previously stored cookies at any time through their browser settings.

After deleting cookies:

* Users may need to sign in again.
* Certain preferences may no longer be remembered.
* The cookie banner may appear again.
* Certain settings may return to their default values.

11.4 Blocking Third-Party Cookies

Most browsers allow users to block only cookies placed by third parties.

This option may reduce analytics tracking without significantly affecting basic website operation.

However, some external services may no longer function correctly.

11.5 Incognito or Private Browsing

Many browsers offer a private or incognito browsing mode.

In this mode:

* Cookies are generally deleted when the window is closed.
* Certain preferences are not retained.
* Users may need to authenticate again during future sessions.

Incognito mode does not necessarily prevent third parties from collecting information under their own policies.

11.6 Consequences of Blocking Cookies

Disabling certain cookies may result in:

* Inability to sign in.
* Loss of personalized preferences.
* Errors during checkout.
* Problems with subscriptions.
* Limited operation of the private account area.
* A reduced browsing experience.

Prompt Studio recommends keeping strictly necessary cookies enabled.

11.7 Management Through Prompt Studio

Where available, Prompt Studio will provide a panel allowing users to:

* Review cookie categories.
* Change consent preferences.
* Enable or disable optional cookies.
* View updated information about each category.

Changes will apply subject to the technical limitations of each browser and provider.

11.8 Updating Preferences

Users may update their cookie preferences at any time.

Prompt Studio will respect those preferences whenever technically possible and in accordance with applicable law.

