Section 16. Retention of Information Obtained Through Cookies

Prompt Studio retains information obtained through cookies only for the period necessary to fulfill the purposes described in this Policy or for the period required by applicable law.

The duration depends on the type and purpose of each cookie.

16.1 Session Cookies

Session cookies remain active only while the user maintains an open browsing session.

They are generally deleted automatically when:

* The browser is closed.
* The user signs out.
* The authenticated session ends.

16.2 Persistent Cookies

Persistent cookies remain stored for a specified period to remember preferences or facilitate future visits.

Their duration may range from a few days to several months or years, depending on their purpose.

16.3 Retention by Providers

When cookies are managed by third parties, the retention period is determined by the relevant provider in accordance with its own policies.

Prompt Studio recommends reviewing those providers’ privacy policies for detailed information about their retention periods.

16.4 Automatic Deletion

Once the purpose for which they were placed has been fulfilled, cookies:

* Will expire automatically.
* Will be replaced where applicable.
* Or may be deleted by the user through browser settings.

16.5 Retention for Legal Obligations

In certain cases, information derived from cookies may be retained for an additional period when necessary to:

* Comply with legal obligations.
* Respond to requests from competent authorities.
* Resolve disputes.
* Defend legal rights.
* Investigate security incidents.

16.6 Anonymized Information

Prompt Studio may retain anonymized statistical information obtained through analytics tools.

Once irreversibly anonymized, this information will no longer be considered personal data under applicable law.

16.7 Security Measures

During the retention period, Prompt Studio will implement reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect information against:

* Unauthorized access.
* Alteration.
* Disclosure.
* Loss.
* Destruction.
* Misuse.

16.8 Data Minimization

Prompt Studio applies the principle of data minimization and will seek to retain only the information strictly necessary to fulfill the purposes described in this Policy, deleting or anonymizing data when it is no longer needed.

